<title>FINLAND: RAISIO SAYS U.S. COOP STILL NEEDS GOVT OK.</title>
<headline>RAISIO SAYS U.S. COOP STILL NEEDS GOVT OK.</headline>
<dateline>HELSINKI 1997-07-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Finnish food group Raision Tehtaat said in a statement on Monday its cooperation agreement with U.S. Johnson &amp; Johnson company McNeil still needed approval from U.S. competition authorities.</p>
<p>&quot;The matter is still in governmental process and no decisions have yet been made,&quot; it said, commenting on a report in daily Kauppalehti which said the deal had been approved.</p>
<p>--Helsinki newsroom +358-9-680 50 245, news@reuters.fi</p>
